From f57433d8350b76cd417920438bf65b9807d8c8ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:16:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/23] BananaDS: tests/irqmask and tests/bigcode; 0023 covers
 self loops, 0022 tells slice ends apart

tests/irqmask: work with CPSR.I set while IRQs are pending (HBlank every line, VBlank, two fast timers): masked
sections with calls, returns, function pointers, loops, IME/IE changes, a supervisor-mode stretch, a CP15 halt;
VBlank's handler loops in IRQ mode, timer 1's nests; the handler hashes a progress counter, so when each IRQ is
taken shows in RAM and on screen. Thumb, ARM, and Thumb with a busy ARM7 masking its own fast timer IRQ. With
jit.irqchain=off it makes ~25k masked-IRQ returns to the loop a frame (ARM9), 0 with it on; pictures and main RAM
identical both ways. tests/bigcode: a game-sized code footprint (500 generated functions by default, all called
each pass in a shuffled order: ~100 KB of Thumb, ~7.7k JIT blocks, ~1.5 MB of JIT code) for instruction-fetch
(L1I/iTLB) measurements that cpubench's few hot loops can't show.

melonDS 0023 now also goes round a self loop's inline check on a masked IRQ (NZCV untouched); 0022 counts a
return at the slice's end with an IRQ masked apart from one the IRQ caused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PvbFhKAw3ERk5a13S651g1
